  "title": "The Second World War, Genocide and the Nuclear Age",
  "summary": "The Second World War intensified total war and demonstrated that modern state capacity could be used for production, mobilization, control and mass violence. Genocide exposed the destructive use of administrative and technical capacity when restraints fail, while nuclear weapons changed the upper bounds of military escalation.",
